	// and make the phone worse for every other element too. Caps at the floor still read as a label
	// because of the tracking; caps below it would just be the new floor.
	// NOWRAP, and the box is allowed to be too small for the text.
	//
	// The box is still exactly the run's leg, so the text still centres on the arrow — that part has
	// to stay. But the leg is derived from the middle column, and the middle went from 560 units to
	// 310 when the stages became two rows of two, which took the leg from 212 to 79. "Views and
	// alerts" needs 143 units set in caps, so it broke over three lines and read as a paragraph
	// floating above an arrow.
	//
	// Overflowing a centred box is symmetric, so the text keeps its centre and simply runs wider than
